Z||000004||Formula||01-22-2000||06:12 PM||||12"..........hmmmmmmmm......<P>I had a 10" explode up front where the spare tire goes......<P>Now I don't (list of reasons why my fiero doesn't like subs)<P>1. The interior rattles now, it used to feel real sturdy but now if squeaks.<P>2. It wasn't very loud inside the car, but you could here it for several hundred yards away.<P>3. I used to have an exhaust leak, Now I don't and the V6 sounds awesome. (no sub needed for cool noise)<P>4. The opposite sex always told me to turn down the bass.<P>5. I have a spare tire again.<P>6. I felt like a rice burner with bass.<P>7. Monkeyman in 2004<P>8. Fieros rule<P>9. hmmmmm<P>10. I saw someplace where you can take the board in front of the firewall out and make an enclosure there.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Spyder||01-22-2000||06:25 PM||||I have the logical answer:<BR>Since I am not familiar with the Saphire sub,<BR>Measure the box you have now, and figure the inside cubic feet then build the new box to have the same cubic feet.  Build the box similar to the drawing in the other post, and put the port firing up toward the ceiling. If you can’t quite build it to that specs add the poly-fill it could help a little.<P>I am about to add two 12” subs behind the seats in my Fiero. I removed the carpeting in front of the fire wall (that almost  gives an inch there) There is a section of metal about 6x12 that can be removed. I removed that section and I have fiberglassed it in. that gives about two inches.  First time Fiberglassing.  First side looks like crap, the second side looks good. I have a bit more room than most Fieros because I took the computer out and the rear glove box.  That’s where I am at now. The main thing the cut out will do is be a place for the speakers magnet.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Spyder (edited 01-22-2000).]||||reg||1
